WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.133 --> 00:00:02.873
I do as they tell me
and the street is safe.

2
00:00:02.923 --> 00:00:04.233
Who are they?

3
00:00:04.283 --> 00:00:07.313
I never meant for anyone to get hurt.

4
00:00:07.363 --> 00:00:09.163
Let me be brave.

5
00:00:10.803 --> 00:00:13.033
Is it a trap? Is it a torture chamber?

6
00:00:13.083 --> 00:00:16.073
If you want any part of killing
her and you're not afraid.

7
00:00:16.123 --> 00:00:18.793
then you understand nothing at all.

8
00:00:23.083 --> 00:00:24.593
'Go to the city.'

9
00:00:24.643 --> 00:00:26.673
Tell them I'm back.

10
00:00:26.723 --> 00:00:29.323
Tell them... I know what they did.

11
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:37.074
Do you want subtitles for any video?
-=[ ai.OpenSubtitles.com ]=-

12
00:01:15.043 --> 00:01:17.273
# Don't stop me now

13
00:01:17.323 --> 00:01:19.913
# I'm having such a good time

14
00:01:19.963 --> 00:01:21.873
# I'm having a ball... #

15
00:01:21.923 --> 00:01:23.283
Hi.

16
00:01:24.843 --> 00:01:26.353
What can I get you?

17
00:01:26.403 --> 00:01:28.543
I don't have any money.

18
00:01:29.803 --> 00:01:31.343
But I play.

19
00:01:33.083 --> 00:01:34.223
OK.

20
00:01:39.243 --> 00:01:41.953
Don't you need to plug that thing in?

21
00:01:42.003 --> 00:01:43.273
Yeah.

22
00:01:47.803 --> 00:01:49.543
You're English.

23
00:01:50.403 --> 00:01:51.943
You're not.

24
00:01:53.163 --> 00:01:55.963
- How did you get out here?
- Magic.

25
00:01:56.803 --> 00:01:59.753
Or... maybe I went to an
airport and caught a plane.

26
00:01:59.803 --> 00:02:01.193
Ah.

27
00:02:01.243 --> 00:02:02.443
You?

28
00:02:04.203 --> 00:02:05.473
Magic.

29
00:02:12.763 --> 00:02:14.433
I believe you.

30
00:02:18.163 --> 00:02:19.633
You been travelling?

31
00:02:19.683 --> 00:02:21.823
Yeah. from time to time.

32
00:02:30.563 --> 00:02:32.713
Is it a sad song?

33
00:02:32.763 --> 00:02:34.553
Nothing's sad till it's over.

34
00:02:34.603 --> 00:02:36.543
Then everything is.

35
00:02:41.763 --> 00:02:43.563
What's it called?

36
00:02:46.043 --> 00:02:48.113
I think that it's called...

37
00:02:48.163 --> 00:02:49.563
.. Clara.

38
00:02:51.003 --> 00:02:52.873
Tell me about her.

39
00:04:15.923 --> 00:04:17.663
Lord President?

40
00:04:18.083 --> 00:04:19.673
Are all the bells ringing?

41
00:04:19.723 --> 00:04:21.663
The whole cloister?

42
00:04:22.163 --> 00:04:24.433
What's going on down there?

43
00:04:26.283 --> 00:04:28.673
On my way down to the Matrix now. sir.

44
00:04:28.723 --> 00:04:31.673
"Keep the perimeter. It's OK to
be afraid down there. soldier."

45
00:04:31.723 --> 00:04:34.513
Sliders are everywhere.
sir. Loads of the things.

46
00:04:34.563 --> 00:04:36.953
"Language. please. I'm
with the President."

47
00:04:37.003 --> 00:04:39.433
Sorry. sir. The Cloister
Wraiths are active.

48
00:04:39.483 --> 00:04:42.433
Do not approach them. don't even
enter the cloister. just tell me.

49
00:04:42.483 --> 00:04:44.233
"are all the bells ringing?"

50
00:04:44.283 --> 00:04:45.713
Yes. sir.

51
00:04:45.763 --> 00:04:47.993
Then we are facing great danger.

52
00:04:48.043 --> 00:04:50.193
The Cloister Wraiths seem to think so.

53
00:04:50.243 --> 00:04:52.043
So. where is he?

54
00:04:52.603 --> 00:04:53.953
Where has the Doctor gone?

55
00:04:54.003 --> 00:04:55.993
Back to the beginning. I should think.

56
00:04:56.043 --> 00:04:59.753
The Sisterhood of Karn has
no business in this chamber.

57
00:04:59.803 --> 00:05:01.433
or on this planet.

58
00:05:01.483 --> 00:05:03.633
I heard the Doctor had come home.

59
00:05:03.683 --> 00:05:05.823
One so loves fireworks!

60
00:05:41.963 --> 00:05:45.553
Why are they ringing all the
bells? Never heard so many.

61
00:05:45.603 --> 00:05:49.403
What's gone wrong this time? All
the fuss they're always making.

62
00:05:50.643 --> 00:05:53.073
You. up there! You're not
supposed to be there!

63
00:05:53.123 --> 00:05:54.473
I've just put all that back.

64
00:05:54.523 --> 00:05:58.163
it's for the boys. if any
of them ever want to come...

65
00:06:08.123 --> 00:06:09.923
They'll kill you.

66
00:06:54.883 --> 00:06:56.033
'Attention!

67
00:06:56.083 --> 00:07:00.183
'Will all non-military personnel
step away from the Doctor.'

68
00:07:03.243 --> 00:07:04.793
I repeat...

69
00:07:04.843 --> 00:07:09.113
all non-military personnel.
please. step away from the Doctor.

70
00:07:09.163 --> 00:07:12.163
'At least move the children away!'

71
00:07:13.883 --> 00:07:17.553
Doctor. you will lay down
any weapons on your person

72
00:07:17.603 --> 00:07:20.143
and accompany us to the capital.

73
00:07:41.923 --> 00:07:45.223
'Doctor. you will accompany
us to the capital.'

74
00:08:03.283 --> 00:08:05.083
'Doctor?'

75
00:08:07.803 --> 00:08:09.393
Come back.

76
00:08:09.443 --> 00:08:10.993
You will come back immediately.

77
00:08:11.043 --> 00:08:14.543
'That is an order and this
is a military vehicle.'

78
00:08:21.403 --> 00:08:23.233
What's his plan?

79
00:08:23.283 --> 00:08:25.823
I think he's finishing his soup.

80
00:08:27.563 --> 00:08:29.513
Suggestion. sir...

81
00:08:29.563 --> 00:08:31.793
'We could talk to him.'

82
00:08:31.843 --> 00:08:33.983
'Words are his weapons.'

83
00:08:34.523 --> 00:08:37.063
'When did they stop being ours?'

84
00:09:08.563 --> 00:09:10.433
Welcome home. sir.

85
00:09:10.963 --> 00:09:13.833
As commander of the armed
forces of Gallifrey.

86
00:09:13.883 --> 00:09:17.283
I bring you the greetings
of the High Council

87
00:09:23.203 --> 00:09:26.313
'Who the hell does he think he is?'

88
00:09:26.363 --> 00:09:28.963
The man who won the Time War. sir.

89
00:09:55.363 --> 00:09:57.163
What is he doing?

90
00:10:02.963 --> 00:10:04.833
What does he want?

91
00:10:05.643 --> 00:10:07.233
Revenge?

92
00:10:07.283 --> 00:10:10.593
The Doctor does not blame Gallifrey
for the horrors of the Time War.

93
00:10:10.643 --> 00:10:12.513
I should hope not.

94
00:10:13.163 --> 00:10:15.563
He just blames you.

95
00:11:25.523 --> 00:11:27.883
Get off my planet.

96
00:11:29.163 --> 00:11:31.123
We needed to know.

97
00:11:32.563 --> 00:11:34.913
You have information about the Hybrid.

98
00:11:34.963 --> 00:11:37.113
A danger to all of us.

99
00:11:37.163 --> 00:11:39.873
If you'd told us what you knew.
you could've walked out of there.

100
00:11:39.923 --> 00:11:41.923
Get off my planet.

101
00:11:44.643 --> 00:11:46.273
You have nothing. Doctor.

102
00:11:46.323 --> 00:11:47.723
Nothing!

103
00:11:48.843 --> 00:11:52.073
Do you know what I have.
out here in the Dry Lands.

104
00:11:52.123 --> 00:11:54.593
where there's nobody who matters?

105
00:11:54.643 --> 00:11:56.443
No witnesses.

106
00:11:58.563 --> 00:12:00.203
Me. too.

107
00:12:01.923 --> 00:12:03.363
Take aim!

108
00:12:04.803 --> 00:12:06.673
Aim at the Doctor.

109
00:12:08.683 --> 00:12:11.083
- Fire on my command.
- Sir?

110
00:12:11.643 --> 00:12:14.553
Step forward and take aim!

111
00:12:14.603 --> 00:12:16.193
What's the matter with you?

112
00:12:16.243 --> 00:12:19.003
Lord President... he's a war hero.

113
00:12:20.123 --> 00:12:23.523
- Some of these men served with him.
- These men serve me!

114
00:12:25.083 --> 00:12:26.623
All of you!

115
00:12:30.483 --> 00:12:32.283
On my command...

116
00:12:49.003 --> 00:12:50.603
Fire!

117
00:12:55.043 --> 00:12:57.313
'Could I have a lemonade?'

118
00:12:58.643 --> 00:13:01.443
Oh. you like a cliffhanger. don't you?

119
00:13:02.643 --> 00:13:05.513
So you went back to your home town...

120
00:13:05.563 --> 00:13:07.153
Something like that.

121
00:13:07.203 --> 00:13:09.073
Glasgow?

122
00:13:09.123 --> 00:13:11.393
Er. well. sort of Glasgow. Space Glasgow.

123
00:13:11.443 --> 00:13:15.113
And there was this gang boss
and he wanted to kill you.

124
00:13:15.163 --> 00:13:16.963
Wanted to. yeah.

125
00:13:33.363 --> 00:13:34.903
You missed!

126
00:13:36.523 --> 00:13:37.593
All of you!

127
00:13:37.643 --> 00:13:40.473
Every single one of you!
How is that possible?

128
00:13:40.523 --> 00:13:42.473
What is it?

129
00:13:42.511 --> 00:13:46.551
Is the firing squad
afraid of the unarmed man?

130
00:13:48.031 --> 00:13:50.031
You... explain.

131
00:13:51.351 --> 00:13:53.621
There was a saying. sir. in the Time War.

132
00:13:53.671 --> 00:13:54.861
A saying?

133
00:13:54.911 --> 00:13:58.391
The first thing you will notice
about the Doctor of War...

134
00:13:59.511 --> 00:14:01.451
.. is he's unarmed.

135
00:14:01.951 --> 00:14:04.351
For many. it's also the last.

136
00:14:27.391 --> 00:14:29.591
I was at Skull Moon. sir.

137
00:14:32.431 --> 00:14:34.581
Is this a story or did this really happen?

138
00:14:34.631 --> 00:14:37.471
Every story ever told really happened.

139
00:14:38.991 --> 00:14:42.591
Stories... are where memories
go when they're forgotten.

140
00:14:50.551 --> 00:14:53.651
Not one more of you
moves! That is an order!

141
00:14:54.431 --> 00:14:57.031
A direct order of your President!

142
00:15:01.031 --> 00:15:03.431
You leave me no choice.

143
00:15:05.111 --> 00:15:08.151
How many regenerations did we grant you?

144
00:15:09.111 --> 00:15:11.051
I've got all night.

145
00:15:14.511 --> 00:15:17.621
Excellent. General. You
sent for reinforcements.

146
00:15:17.671 --> 00:15:19.341
No. he didn't.

147
00:15:22.151 --> 00:15:23.591
I did.

148
00:15:33.151 --> 00:15:34.501
What?

149
00:15:34.551 --> 00:15:36.351
I am Rassilon...

150
00:15:37.071 --> 00:15:38.871
.. the redeemer!

151
00:15:40.751 --> 00:15:43.181
Rassilon. the resurrected!

152
00:15:43.231 --> 00:15:46.031
Gallifrey is mine!

153
00:15:47.911 --> 00:15:49.711
Lord President...

154
00:15:50.591 --> 00:15:52.461
.. with respect...

155
00:15:52.751 --> 00:15:54.821
.. get off his planet.

156
00:16:14.791 --> 00:16:16.461
Gallifrey is currently positioned

157
00:16:16.511 --> 00:16:19.551
at the extreme end of the time
continuum. for its own protection.

158
00:16:21.031 --> 00:16:22.861
We're at the end of the universe.

159
00:16:22.911 --> 00:16:24.781
give or take a star system.

160
00:16:24.831 --> 00:16:26.061
I know.

161
00:16:26.111 --> 00:16:28.381
I came the long way round.

162
00:16:29.791 --> 00:16:32.791
The President may not find anywhere to go.

163
00:16:35.951 --> 00:16:38.221
He's not the President any more.

164
00:16:38.271 --> 00:16:40.411
He was a good man once.

165
00:16:41.071 --> 00:16:44.141
Isn't this... going a little far?

166
00:16:44.191 --> 00:16:46.421
Oh. I've barely started.

167
00:16:46.471 --> 00:16:50.031
Tell the High Council
they're on the next shuttle.

168
00:17:05.831 --> 00:17:08.061
I thought I'd find you down here.

169
00:17:08.111 --> 00:17:09.671
Old times.

170
00:17:12.511 --> 00:17:14.181
You're a long way from Karn.

171
00:17:14.231 --> 00:17:17.791
At the end of everything. one must
expect the company of immortals.

172
00:17:19.111 --> 00:17:20.701
Do you know what they did to me?

173
00:17:20.751 --> 00:17:24.221
A confession dial is a
ritual act of purification.

174
00:17:24.271 --> 00:17:27.621
It allows a dying Time Lord to
face his demons and make his peace.

175
00:17:27.671 --> 00:17:30.671
before his mind is uploaded to the Matrix.

176
00:17:31.711 --> 00:17:34.461
It was never intended as a
torture chamber for the living.

177
00:17:34.511 --> 00:17:38.381
Rassilon grew concerned about
the coming of the Hybrid.

178
00:17:38.431 --> 00:17:42.261
- Afraid! - You were entrapped
and imprisoned at his command.

179
00:17:42.311 --> 00:17:44.421
And look at him now.

180
00:17:44.471 --> 00:17:46.941
Why did you banish him? Was it punishment?

181
00:17:46.991 --> 00:17:48.861
Or for your own protection?

182
00:17:48.911 --> 00:17:51.251
Or are you just being cruel?

183
00:17:51.631 --> 00:17:53.301
Or just being cowardly?

184
00:17:53.351 --> 00:17:55.291
Let's see. shall we?

185
00:17:56.591 --> 00:18:00.181
If you wanted to know about the
Hybrid. why didn't you just ask me?

186
00:18:00.231 --> 00:18:02.381
If the Hybrid is a threat
to the people of this world.

187
00:18:02.431 --> 00:18:03.901
why don't you just tell us?

188
00:18:03.951 --> 00:18:06.151
What do you know already?

189
00:18:07.591 --> 00:18:10.391
- The Hybrid is a legendary...
- No.

190
00:18:10.911 --> 00:18:14.941
The Hybrid is a creature thought to
be crossbred from two warrior races.

191
00:18:14.991 --> 00:18:16.591
Which races?

192
00:18:17.471 --> 00:18:19.461
The Daleks and the Time
Lords. it is supposed.

193
00:18:19.511 --> 00:18:21.101
Oh. must be well hard. then.

194
00:18:21.151 --> 00:18:22.901
Unstoppable.

195
00:18:22.951 --> 00:18:24.461
According to the stories.

196
00:18:24.511 --> 00:18:27.581
If they're just stories.
why are you so worried?

197
00:18:27.631 --> 00:18:30.021
Some Matrix prophecies suggest...

198
00:18:30.071 --> 00:18:32.071
No.

199
00:18:33.951 --> 00:18:36.621
- Many prophesies suggest...
- No.

200
00:18:39.991 --> 00:18:43.301
All... Matrix prophecies concur

201
00:18:43.351 --> 00:18:47.661
that this creature will one day
stand in the ruins of Gallifrey.

202
00:18:47.711 --> 00:18:50.301
It will unravel the web of time

203
00:18:50.351 --> 00:18:53.661
and destroy a billion billion
hearts to heal its own.

204
00:18:53.711 --> 00:18:55.581
What colour is it?

205
00:18:56.791 --> 00:18:57.941
I don't know.

206
00:18:57.991 --> 00:19:00.661
Prophecies. they never tell
you anything useful. do they?

207
00:19:00.711 --> 00:19:02.501
This is no time to play the fool.

208
00:19:02.551 --> 00:19:05.141
It's the end of the universe.
It's the only time I've got.

209
00:19:05.191 --> 00:19:07.781
- And you want me to keep
you all safe. - Can you?

210
00:19:07.831 --> 00:19:10.101
I'll need help. obviously.

211
00:19:10.151 --> 00:19:11.781
Gallifrey is at your command.

212
00:19:11.831 --> 00:19:14.831
Oh. not from you lot. No. you'd
cramp my style. Look at your hats.

213
00:19:17.031 --> 00:19:20.901
I'm going to need the use of an
extraction chamber. to talk...

214
00:19:20.951 --> 00:19:22.871
to an old friend.

215
00:19:34.031 --> 00:19:35.901
Let me be brave...

216
00:19:52.271 --> 00:19:54.221
This way.

217
00:19:54.271 --> 00:19:56.011
I can save you.

218
00:20:18.351 --> 00:20:20.501
- Doctor? - Yeah. - Where am I?

219
00:20:20.551 --> 00:20:22.741
- Is this the TARDIS?
- No.

220
00:20:22.791 --> 00:20:25.101
- This is a planet.
- What planet?

221
00:20:25.151 --> 00:20:26.541
Basically. my place.

222
00:20:26.591 --> 00:20:29.391
I was about to die. I should be dead.

223
00:20:29.951 --> 00:20:31.861
Forget about that. It doesn't matter.

224
00:20:31.911 --> 00:20:33.221
- Hang on. your place?
- Yeah.

225
00:20:33.271 --> 00:20:34.901
- What do you mean. your place?
- My place.

226
00:20:34.951 --> 00:20:36.261
- You don't mean...?
- Yeah.

227
00:20:36.311 --> 00:20:37.541
Gallifrey...

228
00:20:37.591 --> 00:20:39.061
Gallifrey.

229
00:20:40.391 --> 00:20:41.781
OK. Er...

230
00:20:41.831 --> 00:20:43.301
Hang on. Wait. What?

231
00:20:43.351 --> 00:20:44.821
What? Did I miss something?

232
00:20:44.871 --> 00:20:46.861
Well. we're several billion
years in the future

233
00:20:46.911 --> 00:20:49.381
and the universe is pretty much
over. so. yeah. quite a lot.

234
00:20:49.431 --> 00:20:51.701
Young lady. Miss Oswald...

235
00:20:51.751 --> 00:20:55.351
I'm afraid we only have a
very few minutes with you.

236
00:20:57.231 --> 00:20:58.421
Who's he?

237
00:20:58.471 --> 00:21:00.821
According to the Doctor. you
can tell us something about

238
00:21:00.871 --> 00:21:02.501
the creature known as the Hybrid.

239
00:21:02.551 --> 00:21:03.781
Oh...

240
00:21:03.831 --> 00:21:06.101
- Oh. that's weird. What's
wrong with my ears? - Nothing.

241
00:21:06.151 --> 00:21:09.581
- Oh. it's weird. Everything sounds wrong.
- It's a side effect.

242
00:21:09.631 --> 00:21:11.701
I can hear you. I can
hear you fine. It's like...

243
00:21:11.751 --> 00:21:13.541
I don't know. it's like. erm...

244
00:21:13.591 --> 00:21:15.541
It's like something's missing.

245
00:21:15.591 --> 00:21:17.901
Doctor. we have to tell
her. We always tell them.

246
00:21:17.951 --> 00:21:20.951
Tell me what? What's he
talking about? Doctor...?

247
00:21:26.711 --> 00:21:28.851
Doctor. what's going on?

248
00:21:29.631 --> 00:21:32.541
Clara. there's a sound you've been
living with every day of your life.

249
00:21:32.591 --> 00:21:35.061
but you've learned not to hear.

250
00:21:36.111 --> 00:21:37.651
What sound?

251
00:21:38.631 --> 00:21:40.261
What's wrong? Just tell me.

252
00:21:40.311 --> 00:21:41.981
Doctor. what sound?

253
00:21:42.031 --> 00:21:43.771
Your heartbeat.

254
00:21:46.631 --> 00:21:49.931
Your physical processes
have been time looped...

255
00:21:50.711 --> 00:21:53.711
Frozen between one heartbeat and the next.

256
00:21:55.871 --> 00:21:58.611
Even your breathing is just a habit.

257
00:21:59.111 --> 00:22:00.981
You don't need it.

258
00:22:04.111 --> 00:22:06.381
If I'm frozen. how can I...

259
00:22:07.511 --> 00:22:08.781
How can I be walking about?

260
00:22:08.831 --> 00:22:12.261
Because the Time Lords are
very clever. It doesn't matter.

261
00:22:12.311 --> 00:22:14.021
Yes. it matters to me!

262
00:22:14.071 --> 00:22:16.061
Doctor. we have to explain.

263
00:22:16.111 --> 00:22:17.501
Doctor. what is going on?

264
00:22:17.551 --> 00:22:19.781
Although you are currently
conscious and aware.

265
00:22:19.831 --> 00:22:22.621
in fact. you died billions of years ago.

266
00:22:22.671 --> 00:22:24.181
Doctor...?

267
00:22:24.231 --> 00:22:26.221
We have extracted you

268
00:22:26.271 --> 00:22:29.261
at the very end of your time
stream to request your help.

269
00:22:29.311 --> 00:22:33.501
Once we're finished here. you will
be returned to your final moments.

270
00:22:33.551 --> 00:22:37.181
Your death is an
established historical event

271
00:22:37.231 --> 00:22:39.141
and cannot be altered.

272
00:22:39.191 --> 00:22:41.701
- I'm sorry.
- Doctor. will you just talk to me!

273
00:22:41.751 --> 00:22:43.021
I'll try not to break your jaw.

274
00:22:43.071 --> 00:22:45.871
- My jaw?
- I wasn't talking to you.

275
00:22:48.911 --> 00:22:51.261
Doctor. you can't do
this. You know you can't.

276
00:22:51.311 --> 00:22:52.861
No. General. I don't know that.

277
00:22:52.911 --> 00:22:56.101
Everybody. stay exactly where you are!

278
00:22:56.151 --> 00:22:59.261
No moving about. On pain of
death. no-one take a selfie!

279
00:22:59.311 --> 00:23:01.221
These people are unarmed.

280
00:23:01.271 --> 00:23:02.861
So are you.

281
00:23:02.911 --> 00:23:05.421
Doctor. I will not let you leave here.

282
00:23:05.471 --> 00:23:09.541
That's the sidearm of the
President's personal security.

283
00:23:09.591 --> 00:23:11.861
There isn't a stun setting.

284
00:23:12.751 --> 00:23:14.701
I will not let Clara die.

285
00:23:14.751 --> 00:23:17.821
She's been dead for half the
lifetime of the universe.

286
00:23:17.871 --> 00:23:21.831
If you tried to change that.
you could fracture time itself.

287
00:23:23.031 --> 00:23:26.151
Doctor. Lord President. are you
really going to take that risk?

288
00:23:29.951 --> 00:23:31.351
Doctor...

289
00:23:34.591 --> 00:23:36.631
Please...

290
00:23:38.191 --> 00:23:40.061
I don't want this.

291
00:23:43.271 --> 00:23:44.941
Put it down. please.

292
00:23:44.991 --> 00:23:46.591
Regeneration?

293
00:23:48.991 --> 00:23:50.351
Tenth.

294
00:23:51.311 --> 00:23:52.781
Good luck.

295
00:23:53.471 --> 00:23:55.071
You too. sir.

296
00:23:56.111 --> 00:23:58.111
I want a neuro block.

297
00:23:58.671 --> 00:24:01.341
Human compatible. Quickly! Come on!

298
00:24:01.751 --> 00:24:03.491
Come on. quick!

299
00:24:04.551 --> 00:24:07.651
This Clara person. you
must really like her.

300
00:24:08.031 --> 00:24:09.971
Why do you say that?

301
00:24:10.151 --> 00:24:12.141
You killed a man.

302
00:24:12.191 --> 00:24:14.331
You don't seem the type.

303
00:24:15.351 --> 00:24:17.821
You killed that man!
You shot him! He's dead!

304
00:24:17.871 --> 00:24:19.821
- It was him or you.
- I don't care!

305
00:24:19.871 --> 00:24:20.861
Yeah?

306
00:24:20.911 --> 00:24:23.501
Well. the difference is.
when you die. you stay dead.

307
00:24:23.551 --> 00:24:24.941
So does he!

308
00:24:24.991 --> 00:24:28.141
We're on Gallifrey. Death
is Time Lord for man flu!

309
00:24:28.191 --> 00:24:31.141
Med team to sector 52.
extraction chamber seven.

310
00:24:31.191 --> 00:24:33.391
Regeneration in progress.

311
00:24:38.631 --> 00:24:40.771
Are you all right. sir?

312
00:24:43.271 --> 00:24:45.711
Oh... Er. sorry... ma'am.

313
00:24:47.191 --> 00:24:48.701
Urgh...

314
00:24:48.751 --> 00:24:51.151
Back to normal. am I?

315
00:24:52.191 --> 00:24:54.741
The only time I've been
a man. that last body.

316
00:24:54.791 --> 00:24:57.221
Dear Lord. how do you
cope with all that ego?

317
00:24:57.271 --> 00:24:58.941
Ma'am. where's the Doctor?

318
00:24:58.991 --> 00:25:00.141
The Cloisters.

319
00:25:00.191 --> 00:25:01.781
Where else would he run.

320
00:25:01.831 --> 00:25:04.181
except into the greatest
danger on Gallifrey.

321
00:25:04.231 --> 00:25:06.861
The hell of the Time Lords.

322
00:25:06.911 --> 00:25:10.061
I thought you said Gallifrey
was frozen in another dimension?

323
00:25:10.111 --> 00:25:12.781
- Well. they must have unfrozen
it and come back. - How?

324
00:25:12.831 --> 00:25:15.931
I didn't ask. It would
make them feel clever.

325
00:25:19.391 --> 00:25:21.391
- Happy?
- No.

326
00:25:22.511 --> 00:25:24.981
Tell me what a neural block is.

327
00:25:25.191 --> 00:25:26.981
Never mind.

328
00:25:27.031 --> 00:25:28.221
This way.

329
00:25:28.271 --> 00:25:30.261
What did you mean. human compatible?

330
00:25:30.311 --> 00:25:32.981
So what was it. the thing you took?

331
00:25:33.791 --> 00:25:36.791
There was only one way to keep Clara safe.

332
00:25:37.231 --> 00:25:39.421
I had to wipe some of her memory.

333
00:25:39.471 --> 00:25:40.871
Of what?

334
00:25:42.431 --> 00:25:44.191
Of me.

335
00:25:50.431 --> 00:25:54.141
The Cloister Wraiths.
Sliders. we used to call them.

336
00:25:54.191 --> 00:25:55.781
They guard the Matrix.

337
00:25:55.831 --> 00:25:57.861
- We're safe in here.
- Why?

338
00:25:57.911 --> 00:26:00.301
They only attack if you
make any attempt to leave.

339
00:26:00.351 --> 00:26:01.861
How long are we planning to stay?

340
00:26:01.911 --> 00:26:04.511
Or. actually. if you try to stay.

341
00:26:06.151 --> 00:26:09.651
You realise how well that
conversation went. right?

342
00:26:09.751 --> 00:26:12.551
You're starting to look. er. a bit...

343
00:26:21.631 --> 00:26:24.261
We need to block every
exit from the Cloisters.

344
00:26:24.311 --> 00:26:27.661
Every available man. I
need that place surrounded.

345
00:26:27.711 --> 00:26:29.821
No-one's ever made it
back out of the Cloisters.

346
00:26:29.871 --> 00:26:31.781
Not quite no-one.

347
00:26:31.831 --> 00:26:33.501
This way. I'm fairly sure.

348
00:26:33.551 --> 00:26:35.701
According to the stories.
there's a secret way out.

349
00:26:35.751 --> 00:26:37.821
If you find it. the Sliders let you go.

350
00:26:37.871 --> 00:26:42.231
Ex... term... in... ate!

351
00:26:43.191 --> 00:26:44.581
It's OK.

352
00:26:44.631 --> 00:26:46.571
It's OK. look at it.

353
00:26:47.111 --> 00:26:49.741
Exterminate...

354
00:26:49.791 --> 00:26:51.501
me!

355
00:26:51.551 --> 00:26:52.781
Is it trapped?

356
00:26:52.831 --> 00:26:55.501
Don't worry. it's been neutralised.

357
00:26:56.271 --> 00:26:57.381
Those aren't vines.

358
00:26:57.431 --> 00:27:01.111
In your terms. they're fibre-optic
cables. they're alive and growing.

359
00:27:02.191 --> 00:27:04.541
We're inside the biggest
database in history.

360
00:27:04.591 --> 00:27:08.491
- Sometimes. people are stupid
enough to break in. - And?

361
00:27:08.871 --> 00:27:11.261
It's a database. They get filed.

362
00:27:11.311 --> 00:27:16.951
Ex... term... in... ate...

363
00:27:18.471 --> 00:27:19.541
.. me!

364
00:27:19.591 --> 00:27:22.621
Probably a leftover
from the Cloister Wars.

365
00:27:22.671 --> 00:27:25.501
There's nothing we can do. Come on.

366
00:27:25.551 --> 00:27:27.901
Exterminate... me!

367
00:27:27.951 --> 00:27:31.351
Exterminate... me!

368
00:27:32.711 --> 00:27:34.061
Ex...

369
00:27:34.098 --> 00:27:35.608
.. term...

370
00:27:35.658 --> 00:27:37.248
.. in...

371
00:27:37.298 --> 00:27:38.698
.. ate...

372
00:27:40.738 --> 00:27:42.008
.. me!

373
00:28:01.418 --> 00:28:03.358
Keep away from them!

374
00:28:04.578 --> 00:28:06.368
The Matrix can use them as a defence.

375
00:28:06.418 --> 00:28:09.288
It means the secret exit must be close.

376
00:28:13.618 --> 00:28:15.728
- What's to defend in a crypt?
- It's not just a crypt.

377
00:28:15.778 --> 00:28:17.168
More like a stone circuit board.

378
00:28:17.218 --> 00:28:19.328
This is the Matrix database.

379
00:28:19.378 --> 00:28:22.178
Database? What do you mean. database?

380
00:28:24.378 --> 00:28:25.968
Oh...

381
00:28:26.018 --> 00:28:27.488
Oh?

382
00:28:27.538 --> 00:28:28.528
Oh...

383
00:28:28.578 --> 00:28:30.088
Oh?

384
00:28:30.138 --> 00:28:32.048
Oh...

385
00:28:32.098 --> 00:28:34.048
Looks like the primary service hatch.

386
00:28:34.098 --> 00:28:36.898
- Just have to work out the key. - Oh.

387
00:28:38.458 --> 00:28:39.568
When Time Lords die.

388
00:28:39.618 --> 00:28:42.648
their minds are uploaded to
a thing called the Matrix.

389
00:28:42.698 --> 00:28:45.208
This structure. it's
like a living computer.

390
00:28:45.258 --> 00:28:49.888
It can predict the future. generate
prophecies out of algorithms.

391
00:28:49.938 --> 00:28:54.018
ring the Cloister bells in the
event of impending catastrophe.

392
00:28:56.618 --> 00:28:59.808
The Sliders -- they're
just like the guard dogs.

393
00:28:59.858 --> 00:29:01.928
the firewall.

394
00:29:01.978 --> 00:29:04.168
Projections from inside the Matrix itself.

395
00:29:04.218 --> 00:29:07.098
the dead. manning the battlements.

396
00:29:08.738 --> 00:29:10.568
Was I supposed to understand any of that?

397
00:29:10.618 --> 00:29:13.608
The Time Lords have got a
big computer made of ghosts.

398
00:29:13.658 --> 00:29:15.568
in a crypt. guarded by more ghosts.

399
00:29:15.618 --> 00:29:17.088
Didn't hurt. did it?

400
00:29:17.138 --> 00:29:18.618
Tiny bit.

401
00:29:25.298 --> 00:29:28.608
Why would a computer need to protect
itself from the people who made it?

402
00:29:28.658 --> 00:29:31.688
All computers do that in the end.
You wait until the internet starts.

403
00:29:31.738 --> 00:29:34.218
Oh. that was a war!

404
00:29:36.378 --> 00:29:37.808
They don't seem to be moving.

405
00:29:37.858 --> 00:29:40.368
And they're by lift shaft seven.

406
00:29:40.418 --> 00:29:42.218
Keep monitoring.

407
00:29:46.258 --> 00:29:48.528
A long time ago. there was
a student at the Academy.

408
00:29:48.578 --> 00:29:51.578
He got in here. disappeared for four days.

409
00:29:52.258 --> 00:29:54.968
Showed up in a completely
different part of the city.

410
00:29:55.018 --> 00:29:58.408
Said the Sliders talked to him.

411
00:29:58.458 --> 00:30:00.728
they showed him the secret passage out.

412
00:30:00.778 --> 00:30:02.608
And we just need the code.

413
00:30:02.658 --> 00:30:04.648
What. and the kid told you the secret?

414
00:30:04.698 --> 00:30:06.968
Ah. no. he didn't tell anyone anything.

415
00:30:07.018 --> 00:30:09.768
He went completely mad. never right
in the head again. So they say.

416
00:30:09.818 --> 00:30:12.568
- OK. that's encouraging...
- The last I heard.

417
00:30:12.618 --> 00:30:15.778
he stole the moon and
the President's wife.

418
00:30:18.698 --> 00:30:20.088
Was she. erm...

419
00:30:20.138 --> 00:30:22.368
Was she nice. the President's wife?

420
00:30:22.418 --> 00:30:25.328
Ah. well. that was a lie
put about by the Shabogans.

421
00:30:25.378 --> 00:30:28.458
It was the President's daughter. I
didn't steal the moon. I lost it...

422
00:30:29.738 --> 00:30:31.808
I'd know you anywhere.

423
00:30:34.058 --> 00:30:36.648
I was a completely different
person in those days.

424
00:30:36.698 --> 00:30:37.888
Eccentric.

425
00:30:37.938 --> 00:30:39.168
a bit mad.

426
00:30:39.218 --> 00:30:40.728
rude to people.

427
00:30:40.778 --> 00:30:42.608
- Look at me again.
- Sorry. what?

428
00:30:42.658 --> 00:30:45.328
In the eye. Look at me. Just do it.

429
00:30:46.258 --> 00:30:47.528
What?

430
00:30:49.458 --> 00:30:50.998
What is it?

431
00:30:52.978 --> 00:30:55.488
How long has it been for
you since you last saw me?

432
00:30:55.538 --> 00:30:56.568
Oh...

433
00:30:56.618 --> 00:30:59.158
- Oh. I'm not sure.
- How long?

434
00:31:00.458 --> 00:31:03.008
I was stuck on a place.

435
00:31:03.058 --> 00:31:04.448
- They...
- They what?

436
00:31:04.498 --> 00:31:06.208
Who? Who are we talking about?

437
00:31:06.258 --> 00:31:09.258
They wanted something
from me. Information.

438
00:31:10.498 --> 00:31:12.698
It really doesn't matter.

439
00:31:17.378 --> 00:31:19.168
What happened to your coat?

440
00:31:19.218 --> 00:31:21.688
The velvety coat. I
liked that one. it was...

441
00:31:21.738 --> 00:31:23.248
- it was very Doctory.
- I changed it.

442
00:31:23.298 --> 00:31:24.448
Why?

443
00:31:24.498 --> 00:31:27.048
Well. I can't be the Doctor all the time.

444
00:31:27.098 --> 00:31:29.688
I think I've almost got
it. I think this is it.

445
00:31:29.738 --> 00:31:31.288
Tell me what they did to you.

446
00:31:31.338 --> 00:31:34.138
Tell me. what happened to the Doctor?

447
00:31:36.298 --> 00:31:37.648
We're here.

448
00:31:37.698 --> 00:31:39.568
It's pretty quiet.

449
00:31:40.058 --> 00:31:42.168
'He seems to be talking to her.

450
00:31:42.218 --> 00:31:44.168
'Like he's telling her a story.

451
00:31:44.218 --> 00:31:45.688
'You might want to have a look.'

452
00:31:45.738 --> 00:31:47.888
Open up. we're going in.

453
00:31:47.938 --> 00:31:50.808
We'll stick to the perimeter. no
more than three paces from the lift.

454
00:31:50.858 --> 00:31:52.848
Do not enter the Cloisters.

455
00:31:52.898 --> 00:31:55.088
20 feet of pure diamond.

456
00:31:55.138 --> 00:31:57.768
Harder than diamond.

457
00:31:57.818 --> 00:32:00.328
But you break through
anything. given time.

458
00:32:00.378 --> 00:32:01.608
How much time?

459
00:32:01.658 --> 00:32:03.008
- Miss Oswald...
- Stay back.

460
00:32:03.058 --> 00:32:07.298
- I'm sorry. but we have to find a way
to extract you... - I said. stay back!

461
00:32:14.658 --> 00:32:16.848
The Hybrid. what is it?

462
00:32:16.898 --> 00:32:19.008
What's so important you
would fight so long?

463
00:32:19.058 --> 00:32:20.728
It doesn't matter what the Hybrid is.

464
00:32:20.778 --> 00:32:23.048
It only matters that I
convinced them that I knew.

465
00:32:23.098 --> 00:32:25.408
Otherwise. I'd have had
nothing left to bargain with.

466
00:32:25.458 --> 00:32:29.058
- What were you bargaining for?
- What do you think?

467
00:32:29.898 --> 00:32:31.088
You.

468
00:32:31.138 --> 00:32:33.488
I had to find a way to save you.

469
00:32:33.538 --> 00:32:35.048
I knew it had to be the Time Lords.

470
00:32:35.098 --> 00:32:37.008
They cost you your life
on Trap Street. Clara.

471
00:32:37.058 --> 00:32:38.928
and I was going to make
them bring you back.

472
00:32:38.978 --> 00:32:41.488
I just had to hang on in there for a bit.

473
00:32:41.538 --> 00:32:42.968
How long?

474
00:32:43.018 --> 00:32:44.618
It was fine.

475
00:32:48.338 --> 00:32:49.448
One question.

476
00:32:49.498 --> 00:32:50.928
And you will answer.

477
00:32:50.978 --> 00:32:53.648
How long was the Doctor trapped
inside the confession dial?

478
00:32:53.698 --> 00:32:55.048
We think...

479
00:32:55.098 --> 00:32:57.778
four-and-a-half-billion years.

480
00:32:58.898 --> 00:33:00.688
He could have left any time he wanted.

481
00:33:00.738 --> 00:33:02.248
He just had to say what he knew.

482
00:33:02.298 --> 00:33:04.898
The dial would have released him.

483
00:33:20.138 --> 00:33:22.678
Four-and-a-half-billion years...

484
00:33:23.458 --> 00:33:25.198
If she says so.

485
00:33:27.938 --> 00:33:30.208
Why would you even do that?

486
00:33:30.938 --> 00:33:32.768
I was dead!

487
00:33:32.818 --> 00:33:34.168
I was dead and gone.

488
00:33:34.218 --> 00:33:37.318
Why? Why would you even
do that to yourself?

489
00:33:40.178 --> 00:33:42.178
I had a duty of care.

490
00:33:44.538 --> 00:33:47.078
Listen. I'm nearly through here.

491
00:33:48.938 --> 00:33:51.648
If I'm right. there should
be a service duct under here.

492
00:33:51.698 --> 00:33:53.928
We'll be able to get to the old workshops.

493
00:33:53.978 --> 00:33:55.488
They'll have TARDISes there.

494
00:33:55.538 --> 00:33:57.138
OK. listen...

495
00:33:58.498 --> 00:34:01.128
- I have something I need to say.
- We do not have time.

496
00:34:01.178 --> 00:34:02.778
No. my time.

497
00:34:04.658 --> 00:34:05.888
My time is up.

498
00:34:05.938 --> 00:34:09.698
Doctor. between one heartbeat and
the last is all the time I have.

499
00:34:12.658 --> 00:34:14.928
People like me and you.

500
00:34:14.978 --> 00:34:17.888
we should say things to one another.

501
00:34:17.938 --> 00:34:20.478
And I'm going to say them now...

502
00:34:41.938 --> 00:34:43.738
You're monsters.

503
00:34:44.618 --> 00:34:47.728
Here you are. hiding
away at the end of time.

504
00:34:47.778 --> 00:34:49.778
Do you even know why?

505
00:34:50.378 --> 00:34:52.448
Because you are hated.

506
00:34:53.538 --> 00:34:55.098
You are...

507
00:34:56.578 --> 00:34:59.258
.. hated by everybody.

508
00:35:00.338 --> 00:35:02.208
But by nobody more than me.

509
00:35:02.258 --> 00:35:03.928
What did you say to him?

510
00:35:03.978 --> 00:35:05.928
Oh. nothing I'm going to tell you.

511
00:35:05.978 --> 00:35:07.778
or anybody else.

512
00:35:08.538 --> 00:35:10.448
Except. maybe this one part.

513
00:35:10.498 --> 00:35:12.058
I said...

514
00:35:16.138 --> 00:35:18.408
"Don't worry. Doctor.

515
00:35:18.458 --> 00:35:20.928
"They'll all be looking at me!"

516
00:35:23.938 --> 00:35:26.328
You need to tell us what the
Doctor is going to do now.

517
00:35:26.378 --> 00:35:28.088
You really are thick. aren't you?

518
00:35:28.138 --> 00:35:31.088
The Doctor is back on Gallifrey.

519
00:35:31.138 --> 00:35:34.538
Took him four-and-half-billion
years to get here.

520
00:35:35.138 --> 00:35:38.008
What do you think he's going to do now?

521
00:35:39.018 --> 00:35:42.248
Why. he's stealing a
TARDIS and running away.

522
00:35:42.298 --> 00:35:44.058
Bye!

523
00:35:45.298 --> 00:35:46.368
You were quick.

524
00:35:46.418 --> 00:35:48.448
Time machine. I backed up a bit.

525
00:35:48.498 --> 00:35:50.968
'Doctor! Doctor. face me!'

526
00:35:51.018 --> 00:35:52.768
Doctor. can you hear me?

527
00:35:52.818 --> 00:35:56.298
- Get out of that TARDIS
and face me. boy! - Boy?

528
00:36:00.498 --> 00:36:02.248
You have gone too far.

529
00:36:02.298 --> 00:36:05.088
You have broken every
code you ever lived by.

530
00:36:05.138 --> 00:36:08.408
After all this time. after
everything I've done.

531
00:36:08.458 --> 00:36:11.168
- don't you think the universe
owes me this? - Owes you what?

532
00:36:11.218 --> 00:36:12.968
All you're doing is giving her hope.

533
00:36:13.018 --> 00:36:14.728
Since when is hope a bad thing?

534
00:36:14.778 --> 00:36:18.178
Hope is a terrible thing on the scaffold.

535
00:36:27.818 --> 00:36:29.248
Where can he run?

536
00:36:29.298 --> 00:36:31.208
Where he always runs.

537
00:36:31.258 --> 00:36:32.658
Away.

538
00:36:34.738 --> 00:36:36.258
Just away.

539
00:36:38.818 --> 00:36:40.728
- What do you think of
the new wheels? - Basic.

540
00:36:40.778 --> 00:36:44.218
- Classic! Look at the colour
scheme. - It's all white. - Genius!

541
00:36:46.018 --> 00:36:49.088
Check your heartbeat again.

542
00:36:49.138 --> 00:36:52.088
- I think that you'll
find you have one. - Yeah?

543
00:36:52.138 --> 00:36:55.138
It should have restarted when we
broke free of Gallifrey's time zone.

544
00:36:56.618 --> 00:36:58.088
You're alive!

545
00:36:58.138 --> 00:37:00.048
Now we just have to
shake off the Time Lords.

546
00:37:00.098 --> 00:37:01.808
There's only one place we can do that.

547
00:37:01.858 --> 00:37:03.968
What do you say to lunch.
followed by breakfast?

548
00:37:04.018 --> 00:37:06.288
Because we're time travellers
and that's how we roll.

549
00:37:06.338 --> 00:37:09.408
Then cocktails with Moses. Then I'm
going to invent a flying submarine.

550
00:37:09.458 --> 00:37:11.528
Why? Because no-one ever
has and it's annoying.

551
00:37:11.578 --> 00:37:14.528
And maybe we should use this
TARDIS to find my proper one.

552
00:37:14.578 --> 00:37:16.578
I need a clean shirt.

553
00:37:18.218 --> 00:37:19.888
Doctor...

554
00:37:19.938 --> 00:37:21.488
I still don't have a pulse.

555
00:37:21.538 --> 00:37:24.978
- You just haven't found it yet. Try again.
- I know how to take my pulse.

556
00:37:26.138 --> 00:37:28.408
Look. I know how to do it.

557
00:37:29.138 --> 00:37:31.138
See. no pulse. right?

558
00:37:36.858 --> 00:37:38.728
Is it still there?

559
00:37:39.258 --> 00:37:40.408
Don't lie to me.

560
00:37:40.458 --> 00:37:42.648
I think we maybe just have
to fly a little bit further.

561
00:37:42.698 --> 00:37:44.898
give it a bit more welly.

562
00:37:48.498 --> 00:37:50.448
They said. your lot.

563
00:37:50.498 --> 00:37:53.408
that if you saved me. time would
fracture. What does that mean?

564
00:37:53.458 --> 00:37:56.008
Oh. they're exaggerating.

565
00:37:56.058 --> 00:37:58.408
They exaggerate all the time.

566
00:37:58.458 --> 00:38:00.928
History will be fine.

567
00:38:00.978 --> 00:38:03.248
Time will heal. It always does.

568
00:38:03.298 --> 00:38:05.008
- Always?
- Yeah.

569
00:38:05.058 --> 00:38:07.768
It'll sort itself out. It'll be all right.

570
00:38:07.818 --> 00:38:11.718
You'll have a heartbeat. Or
don't you trust me any more?!

571
00:38:11.898 --> 00:38:14.298
No. Not when you're shouting.

572
00:38:21.458 --> 00:38:23.728
- Where are we going?
- Nowhere in space.

573
00:38:23.778 --> 00:38:25.578
forward in time.

574
00:38:28.098 --> 00:38:30.848
We're going to the last
hours of the universe.

575
00:38:30.898 --> 00:38:34.768
We're going long past where
the Time Lords were hiding.

576
00:38:34.818 --> 00:38:36.888
Literally. to the end.

577
00:38:37.258 --> 00:38:39.408
They won't be able to track us there.

578
00:38:39.458 --> 00:38:41.328
We'll just be there for a minute.

579
00:38:41.378 --> 00:38:43.338
I just need to...

580
00:38:45.618 --> 00:38:47.728
I need to make an adjustment.

581
00:38:47.778 --> 00:38:49.168
To what?

582
00:38:49.218 --> 00:38:51.888
It's nothing. really. It's this...

583
00:38:51.938 --> 00:38:53.088
A neural block.

584
00:38:53.138 --> 00:38:56.008
Human compatible. That's what you said.

585
00:38:59.938 --> 00:39:02.478
We don't have to stay here long.

586
00:39:03.218 --> 00:39:05.008
Check your heartbeat again.

587
00:39:05.058 --> 00:39:07.888
Your timeline must have started by now.

588
00:39:07.938 --> 00:39:09.608
A pulse. yeah?

589
00:39:10.818 --> 00:39:12.888
You have a pulse. yes?

590
00:39:13.418 --> 00:39:14.848
Pulse?

591
00:39:14.898 --> 00:39:17.128
- Let me do it.
- I am checking it properly!

592
00:39:17.178 --> 00:39:18.608
This should work.

593
00:39:18.658 --> 00:39:20.778
This has got to work.

594
00:39:21.938 --> 00:39:24.938
What if one last heartbeat
is all I've got?

595
00:39:25.778 --> 00:39:27.688
What if time isn't healing?

596
00:39:27.738 --> 00:39:29.328
What if the universe needs me to die?

597
00:39:29.378 --> 00:39:32.128
The universe is over! It
doesn't have a say any more!

598
00:39:32.178 --> 00:39:34.288
We're standing on the last ember.

599
00:39:34.338 --> 00:39:37.128
the last fragment of
everything that ever was.

600
00:39:37.178 --> 00:39:40.278
As of this moment. I
am answerable to no-one!

601
00:39:54.778 --> 00:39:57.248
How can there be anybody there?

602
00:39:57.858 --> 00:39:59.528
Four knocks...

603
00:40:00.858 --> 00:40:02.998
It's always four knocks.

604
00:40:03.738 --> 00:40:05.058
No.

605
00:40:06.458 --> 00:40:07.968
This one I do alone.

606
00:40:08.018 --> 00:40:10.008
What's out there?

607
00:40:10.058 --> 00:40:11.298
Me.

608
00:40:28.698 --> 00:40:30.568
I told you once...

609
00:40:31.978 --> 00:40:33.778
.. so long ago...

610
00:40:36.578 --> 00:40:40.018
that the universe would become a very
small place when I'm angry with you.

611
00:40:42.738 --> 00:40:44.938
Small enough for you yet?

612
00:40:46.898 --> 00:40:48.458
Hello. me.

613
00:40:49.458 --> 00:40:52.128
You don't seem surprised to see me.

614
00:40:54.138 --> 00:40:55.248
At the end of everything.

615
00:40:55.298 --> 00:40:59.208
we should expect the company
of immortals. so I've been told.

616
00:40:59.258 --> 00:41:01.528
Even the other immortals are gone.

617
00:41:01.578 --> 00:41:03.178
It's just me.

618
00:41:04.978 --> 00:41:06.328
The one and only me.

619
00:41:06.378 --> 00:41:08.008
Finally. you earn the title.

620
00:41:08.058 --> 00:41:11.048
sitting here in a reality bubble
at the end of time itself.

621
00:41:11.098 --> 00:41:13.568
How are you sustaining it. by the way?

622
00:41:13.606 --> 00:41:15.206
Brilliantly.

623
00:41:16.166 --> 00:41:18.766
I've been watching the stars die.

624
00:41:19.566 --> 00:41:21.366
It was beautiful.

625
00:41:24.726 --> 00:41:26.086
No.

626
00:41:27.206 --> 00:41:28.396
It was sad.

627
00:41:28.446 --> 00:41:30.726
No. It was both.

628
00:41:32.566 --> 00:41:36.266
But that's not something
you would understand. is it?

629
00:41:36.526 --> 00:41:38.666
You don't like endings.

630
00:41:40.046 --> 00:41:41.846
She died. Doctor.

631
00:41:43.046 --> 00:41:46.356
Clara died billions of years ago.

632
00:41:46.406 --> 00:41:47.836
- You killed her.
- No.

633
00:41:47.886 --> 00:41:49.596
- You let it happen.
- No. I didn't.

634
00:41:49.646 --> 00:41:51.156
Neither did you.

635
00:41:51.206 --> 00:41:52.796
She did.

636
00:41:52.846 --> 00:41:55.846
She died for who she
was and who she loved.

637
00:41:56.246 --> 00:41:58.476
She fell where she stood. It was sad.

638
00:41:58.526 --> 00:42:00.606
And it was beautiful.

639
00:42:02.206 --> 00:42:03.956
And it is over.

640
00:42:04.006 --> 00:42:06.836
- We have no right to change
who she was. - Ashildr...

641
00:42:06.886 --> 00:42:09.316
- Me.
- Me. go to hell.

642
00:42:09.366 --> 00:42:12.866
By my calculations. you've
got about five minutes.

643
00:42:13.126 --> 00:42:16.116
- You know why we run. Doctor?
- Because it's fun!

644
00:42:16.166 --> 00:42:19.036
Because we know summer can't last forever.

645
00:42:19.086 --> 00:42:21.766
Of course it can. Of course it can.

646
00:42:22.966 --> 00:42:24.756
You just have to steal a time machine.

647
00:42:24.806 --> 00:42:26.346
The Hybrid.

648
00:42:28.446 --> 00:42:32.446
Five minutes to hell. I think
it's time to tell the truth.

649
00:42:46.566 --> 00:42:47.836
Screen on.

650
00:42:47.886 --> 00:42:50.316
'You were barely more than a child.'

651
00:42:50.366 --> 00:42:52.316
You broke in here

652
00:42:52.366 --> 00:42:54.356
and the Wraiths spoke
to you about the Hybrid.

653
00:42:54.406 --> 00:42:56.036
Why did that story make you so scared?

654
00:42:56.086 --> 00:42:57.556
I don't know. I don't remember it.

655
00:42:57.606 --> 00:42:59.516
Sometimes you do.

656
00:42:59.566 --> 00:43:02.316
It's always the way with
things we'd rather forget.

657
00:43:02.366 --> 00:43:04.156
You remember now. though. don't you?

658
00:43:04.206 --> 00:43:07.036
Tell me. Doctor. who is... the Hybrid?

659
00:43:07.086 --> 00:43:09.196
Who threatens all of time and space?

660
00:43:09.246 --> 00:43:10.996
Oh. that's easy. That's very. very easy.

661
00:43:11.046 --> 00:43:12.646
The Hybrid...

662
00:43:13.726 --> 00:43:15.126
is you.

663
00:43:16.886 --> 00:43:19.916
'I'm human. with a little
bit of Mire inside me.'

664
00:43:19.966 --> 00:43:22.356
'The Hybrid is supposed to be
half Time Lord. half Dalek.'

665
00:43:22.406 --> 00:43:23.636
'No. it isn't.'

666
00:43:23.686 --> 00:43:26.756
The actual prophecy specifies
only two warrior races.

667
00:43:26.806 --> 00:43:29.316
The Daleks and the Time Lords
made assumptions. of course.

668
00:43:29.366 --> 00:43:30.596
And they would.

669
00:43:30.646 --> 00:43:33.126
Humans and the Mire...

670
00:43:34.086 --> 00:43:37.086
.. both warrior races. It fits perfectly.

671
00:43:37.606 --> 00:43:39.516
It's an interesting theory.

672
00:43:39.566 --> 00:43:41.766
Do you have a better one?

673
00:43:42.566 --> 00:43:44.476
By your own reasoning.

674
00:43:44.526 --> 00:43:48.566
why couldn't the Hybrid be
half Time Lord. half human?

675
00:43:51.206 --> 00:43:53.236
Tell me. Doctor. I've always wondered...

676
00:43:53.286 --> 00:43:55.116
You're a Time Lord.

677
00:43:55.166 --> 00:43:57.636
you're a high-born Gallifreyan.

678
00:43:58.486 --> 00:44:01.486
Why is it you spend so much time on Earth?

679
00:44:03.606 --> 00:44:05.716
That's your best theory? I'm the Hybrid?

680
00:44:05.766 --> 00:44:08.396
I ran away from Gallifrey
because I was afraid of myself?

681
00:44:08.446 --> 00:44:10.396
That doesn't make any sense.

682
00:44:10.446 --> 00:44:13.386
It makes perfect sense. and you know it.

683
00:44:14.126 --> 00:44:16.116
Am I right?

684
00:44:16.166 --> 00:44:18.076
Is it true?

685
00:44:18.126 --> 00:44:19.866
Does it matter?

686
00:44:22.246 --> 00:44:23.526
No.

687
00:44:25.206 --> 00:44:28.116
Because I have a better theory.

688
00:44:28.166 --> 00:44:29.596
Really?

689
00:44:29.646 --> 00:44:33.566
What if the Hybrid wasn't
one person. but two?

690
00:44:36.726 --> 00:44:39.516
- Two?
- A dangerous combination

691
00:44:39.566 --> 00:44:42.396
of a passionate and powerful Time Lord

692
00:44:42.446 --> 00:44:45.276
and a young woman so very similar to him.

693
00:44:45.326 --> 00:44:48.796
'Companions who are willing to
push each other to extremes.'

694
00:44:48.846 --> 00:44:52.156
She's my friend. She's just my friend.

695
00:44:52.206 --> 00:44:54.196
How did you meet her?

696
00:44:54.246 --> 00:44:55.686
Missy...!

697
00:44:56.756 --> 00:44:57.756
Missy.

698
00:44:57.806 --> 00:44:59.876
Missy.

699
00:44:59.926 --> 00:45:01.466
The Master.

700
00:45:02.566 --> 00:45:04.606
The lover of chaos.

701
00:45:05.686 --> 00:45:07.076
Who wants you to love it. too.

702
00:45:07.126 --> 00:45:09.396
She's quite the matchmaker.

703
00:45:10.166 --> 00:45:11.396
Clara's my friend.

704
00:45:11.446 --> 00:45:12.846
I know.

705
00:45:13.966 --> 00:45:16.316
And you're willing to
risk all of time and space

706
00:45:16.366 --> 00:45:18.366
because you miss her.

707
00:45:19.326 --> 00:45:22.956
- One wonders what the pair of you
will get up to next. - Nothing.

708
00:45:23.006 --> 00:45:24.636
Nothing at all.

709
00:45:24.686 --> 00:45:26.796
I know I went too far.

710
00:45:26.846 --> 00:45:28.396
I get it.

711
00:45:28.446 --> 00:45:30.796
That's why I'm doing what I'm doing.

712
00:45:30.846 --> 00:45:33.316
- And what would that be?
- I'm taking her back to Earth.

713
00:45:33.366 --> 00:45:35.956
Somewhere safe. somewhere out of the way.

714
00:45:36.006 --> 00:45:39.906
I'm going to wipe her memory
of every last detail of me.

715
00:45:40.366 --> 00:45:42.356
'It'll be like our
friendship never happened.'

716
00:45:42.406 --> 00:45:45.006
'That may not be what she wants.'

717
00:45:45.166 --> 00:45:46.916
'I've done it before.

718
00:45:46.966 --> 00:45:48.996
'Usually. I do it telepathically.

719
00:45:49.046 --> 00:45:52.046
'But this time. I've
got something better.'

720
00:45:52.926 --> 00:45:54.876
It's quite...

721
00:45:54.926 --> 00:45:56.436
painless.

722
00:45:56.486 --> 00:45:59.156
Will you tell her what you're going to do?

723
00:45:59.206 --> 00:46:00.196
Of course.

724
00:46:00.246 --> 00:46:01.716
When?

725
00:46:01.766 --> 00:46:02.966
Now.

726
00:46:07.766 --> 00:46:09.306
Screen off.

727
00:46:23.446 --> 00:46:25.316
- You OK?
- Yeah.

728
00:46:26.166 --> 00:46:28.996
Yeah. yeah. Just. you know. my pulse.

729
00:46:29.046 --> 00:46:30.876
Yeah. we'll fix that somehow. I promise.

730
00:46:30.926 --> 00:46:34.406
- You remember Ashildr. of course.
- Yeah. sure.

731
00:46:35.686 --> 00:46:38.786
I thought you'd be more
surprised to see her.

732
00:46:40.326 --> 00:46:42.066
I was watching.

733
00:46:43.046 --> 00:46:44.786
On the monitor.

734
00:46:46.366 --> 00:46:47.956
No.

735
00:46:48.006 --> 00:46:50.596
Doctor. whatever you're
about to do. don't do it!

736
00:46:50.646 --> 00:46:53.676
It won't hurt. it'll be nothing.
You'll just pass out for a moment.

737
00:46:53.726 --> 00:46:55.676
- And then?
- When you wake. you'll be fine.

738
00:46:55.726 --> 00:46:57.596
- But...
- Clara. just listen to me.

739
00:46:57.646 --> 00:46:59.356
Just say it. Say it.

740
00:46:59.406 --> 00:47:00.996
Come on. Tell me.

741
00:47:01.046 --> 00:47:03.076
When you wake up. you
will have forgotten me.

742
00:47:03.126 --> 00:47:05.996
- You'll have forgotten we ever even met.
- And why would I want that?

743
00:47:06.046 --> 00:47:07.236
Because it's the only way.

744
00:47:07.286 --> 00:47:09.276
That stuff in your head. the image of me.

745
00:47:09.326 --> 00:47:11.236
they could use it to find you.

746
00:47:11.286 --> 00:47:13.316
I. er... I used these.

747
00:47:13.366 --> 00:47:14.556
- On what?
- That.

748
00:47:14.606 --> 00:47:16.596
- What did you do?
- What do you think?

749
00:47:16.646 --> 00:47:18.596
Ashildr's right. you see? We're too alike.

750
00:47:18.646 --> 00:47:19.956
- Tell me what you did.
- What else?

751
00:47:20.006 --> 00:47:22.236
What else do you think I
did? I reversed the polarity.

752
00:47:22.286 --> 00:47:24.676
Push that button. Doctor. it
will go off in your own face.

753
00:47:24.726 --> 00:47:26.996
- You were trying to trick me?
- What were you doing to me?

754
00:47:27.046 --> 00:47:29.846
- I'm trying to keep you safe.
- Why?

755
00:47:30.366 --> 00:47:32.116
Nobody's ever safe.

756
00:47:32.166 --> 00:47:34.906
I've never asked you for that. ever.

757
00:47:35.166 --> 00:47:36.916
These have been the best years of my life.

758
00:47:36.966 --> 00:47:38.836
And they are mine.

759
00:47:40.246 --> 00:47:43.756
Tomorrow is promised to no-one.
Doctor. but I insist upon my past.

760
00:47:43.806 --> 00:47:45.876
I am entitled to that.

761
00:47:47.526 --> 00:47:49.406
It's mine.

762
00:47:58.766 --> 00:48:00.846
Oh. Clara Oswald...

763
00:48:04.766 --> 00:48:06.566
What am I doing?

764
00:48:11.846 --> 00:48:13.486
You're right.

765
00:48:15.166 --> 00:48:17.356
You're always...

766
00:48:17.406 --> 00:48:19.006
always right.

767
00:48:21.606 --> 00:48:23.546
So what happens now?

768
00:48:24.326 --> 00:48:25.396
Hey?

769
00:48:25.446 --> 00:48:27.836
Me and you. what do we do now?

770
00:48:27.886 --> 00:48:30.116
I'm not sure you managed
to reverse the polarity.

771
00:48:30.166 --> 00:48:32.636
I'm not even sure that you can.

772
00:48:34.486 --> 00:48:36.036
It'll do something...

773
00:48:36.086 --> 00:48:37.596
to one of us.

774
00:48:37.646 --> 00:48:39.986
Better than flipping a coin.

775
00:48:41.366 --> 00:48:42.966
Doctor...?

776
00:48:45.086 --> 00:48:47.226
You and me... together.

777
00:48:49.766 --> 00:48:51.916
Look how far I went.

778
00:48:51.966 --> 00:48:54.106
for fear of losing you.

779
00:48:56.406 --> 00:48:58.236
This has to stop.

780
00:48:58.286 --> 00:49:00.226
One of us has to go.

781
00:49:14.486 --> 00:49:16.356
You really don't know which?

782
00:49:16.406 --> 00:49:18.146
Let's find out.

783
00:49:18.926 --> 00:49:23.086
Let's do it like we've
done everything else.

784
00:49:24.286 --> 00:49:25.806
Together.

785
00:49:29.286 --> 00:49:31.236
How about we just don't?

786
00:49:31.286 --> 00:49:34.076
Why don't we just... fly away somewhere?

787
00:49:34.126 --> 00:49:36.726
Oh. that'd be great. wouldn't it?

788
00:49:40.206 --> 00:49:41.726
God. yeah.

789
00:49:45.686 --> 00:49:47.486
Good luck. Clara.

790
00:49:48.406 --> 00:49:50.276
Good luck. Doctor.

791
00:49:55.846 --> 00:49:57.846
So. what happens now?

792
00:50:00.966 --> 00:50:03.996
I suppose. we just. erm... We
just wait a minute. I suppose.

793
00:50:04.046 --> 00:50:06.166
And one of us...

794
00:50:11.646 --> 00:50:13.766
One of us will...

795
00:50:15.446 --> 00:50:18.566
I don't think I could ever forget you.

796
00:50:21.166 --> 00:50:24.666
Clara. I don't think you're
ever going to have to.

797
00:50:32.086 --> 00:50:33.366
No...

798
00:50:34.446 --> 00:50:35.636
Run like hell!

799
00:50:35.686 --> 00:50:37.276
What?

800
00:50:37.326 --> 00:50:39.196
Run like hell. because you always need to.

801
00:50:39.246 --> 00:50:41.596
Laugh at everything.
because it's always funny.

802
00:50:41.646 --> 00:50:43.436
No. Stop it. You're saying goodbye.

803
00:50:43.486 --> 00:50:47.436
- Don't say goodbye!
- Never be cruel and never be cowardly.

804
00:50:47.486 --> 00:50:50.686
And if you ever are. always make amends.

805
00:50:52.126 --> 00:50:53.396
Stop it!

806
00:50:53.446 --> 00:50:54.596
Stop! Stop it!

807
00:50:54.646 --> 00:50:56.516
Never eat pears.

808
00:50:56.566 --> 00:50:58.876
They're too squishy and they
always make your chin wet.

809
00:50:58.926 --> 00:51:00.836
That one's quite important. Write it down.

810
00:51:00.886 --> 00:51:02.636
I didn't mean to do this. I'm sorry.

811
00:51:02.686 --> 00:51:04.086
It's OK.

812
00:51:05.606 --> 00:51:07.006
It's OK.

813
00:51:08.046 --> 00:51:09.836
I went too far.

814
00:51:09.886 --> 00:51:11.876
I broke all my own rules.

815
00:51:11.926 --> 00:51:14.116
I became the Hybrid.

816
00:51:14.166 --> 00:51:16.326
This is right.

817
00:51:17.926 --> 00:51:19.526
I accept it.

818
00:51:20.606 --> 00:51:22.206
I can't.

819
00:51:25.006 --> 00:51:27.676
There has to be something I can do.

820
00:51:28.526 --> 00:51:30.126
Smile for me.

821
00:51:30.926 --> 00:51:32.156
Go on.

822
00:51:32.206 --> 00:51:34.236
Clara Oswald...

823
00:51:34.286 --> 00:51:36.126
one last time.

824
00:51:38.886 --> 00:51:40.756
How could I smile?

825
00:51:44.406 --> 00:51:45.806
It's OK.

826
00:51:46.566 --> 00:51:48.366
Don't you worry.

827
00:51:49.086 --> 00:51:50.886
I'll remember it.

828
00:52:09.366 --> 00:52:10.566
Sir?

829
00:52:12.006 --> 00:52:13.876
Are you all right?

830
00:52:15.206 --> 00:52:16.746
Where am I?

831
00:52:21.046 --> 00:52:22.996
How did I get here?

832
00:52:23.046 --> 00:52:24.716
Clara asked me to look after you.

833
00:52:24.766 --> 00:52:27.516
She said you might be a bit... upset.

834
00:52:27.566 --> 00:52:29.836
- Clara?
- Yeah.

835
00:52:29.886 --> 00:52:31.756
She was just here.

836
00:52:32.526 --> 00:52:34.866
I don't know where she went.

837
00:52:35.806 --> 00:52:37.126
Clara?

838
00:52:38.246 --> 00:52:39.846
Clara who?

839
00:52:41.486 --> 00:52:44.396
When something goes missing.
you can always recreate it

840
00:52:44.446 --> 00:52:46.386
by the hole it left.

841
00:52:47.046 --> 00:52:49.156
I know her name was Clara.

842
00:52:49.206 --> 00:52:51.606
I know we travelled together.

843
00:52:51.966 --> 00:52:54.196
I know that there was an
Ice Warrior on a submarine

844
00:52:54.246 --> 00:52:55.996
and a mummy on the Orient Express.

845
00:52:56.046 --> 00:52:58.596
I know we sat together in the Cloisters

846
00:52:58.646 --> 00:53:00.876
and she told me something very important.

847
00:53:00.926 --> 00:53:03.526
but I have no idea what she said.

848
00:53:04.886 --> 00:53:07.026
Or what she looked like.

849
00:53:07.566 --> 00:53:09.676
Or how she talked.

850
00:53:09.726 --> 00:53:11.266
Or laughed.

851
00:53:14.366 --> 00:53:15.796
There's nothing there.

852
00:53:15.846 --> 00:53:17.446
Just nothing.

853
00:53:21.166 --> 00:53:23.306
Are you looking for her?

854
00:53:25.166 --> 00:53:26.706
I'm trying.

855
00:53:27.526 --> 00:53:29.116
She could be anyone. right?

856
00:53:29.166 --> 00:53:31.436
You don't know who you're looking for.

857
00:53:31.486 --> 00:53:34.916
I mean. she could be me. for all you know.

858
00:53:34.966 --> 00:53:38.236
There's one thing I know
about her. Just one thing.

859
00:53:38.286 --> 00:53:41.386
If I met her again. I
would absolutely know.

860
00:53:43.286 --> 00:53:46.486
I think that we were here. you know?

861
00:53:47.726 --> 00:53:50.676
I think that we were here together once.

862
00:53:50.726 --> 00:53:52.866
I'm sure I'll remember.

863
00:53:53.646 --> 00:53:55.166
Over here.

864
00:53:57.526 --> 00:54:00.156
Stupid Doctor... Amy and Rory.

865
00:54:00.206 --> 00:54:02.146
It was Amy and Rory!

866
00:54:03.566 --> 00:54:06.796
What about your TARDIS.
hey? Have you found that yet?

867
00:54:06.846 --> 00:54:08.196
No.

868
00:54:08.246 --> 00:54:11.546
Somebody's moved it from
London. Still looking.

869
00:54:12.926 --> 00:54:14.726
But this diner...

870
00:54:15.846 --> 00:54:18.356
.. it wasn't always here. was it?

871
00:54:18.406 --> 00:54:20.116
It used to be on the
other side of the hill.

872
00:54:20.166 --> 00:54:23.666
Well. maybe someone will
find your TARDIS for you.

873
00:54:39.886 --> 00:54:42.756
What Clara told you in the Cloisters...

874
00:54:44.486 --> 00:54:46.316
I don't remember a single thing about it.

875
00:54:46.366 --> 00:54:47.596
You said memories...

876
00:54:47.646 --> 00:54:49.556
become stories

877
00:54:49.606 --> 00:54:51.546
when we forget them.

878
00:54:53.926 --> 00:54:56.466
Maybe some of them become songs.

879
00:54:58.966 --> 00:55:01.046
That would be nice.

880
00:55:05.086 --> 00:55:07.556
Yeah. it would be. wouldn't it?

881
00:55:52.326 --> 00:55:55.156
I don't think I've got the
Chameleon circuit working.

882
00:55:55.206 --> 00:55:58.676
- The outer shell might be stuck
as an American Diner. - Awesome.

883
00:55:58.726 --> 00:56:00.806
Still no pulse?

884
00:56:03.366 --> 00:56:05.076
Time isn't healing.

885
00:56:05.126 --> 00:56:06.956
I am still frozen.

886
00:56:07.006 --> 00:56:08.236
You know what that means?

887
00:56:08.286 --> 00:56:10.396
It means my death is a fixed event.

888
00:56:10.446 --> 00:56:12.636
The universe depends on it happening.

889
00:56:12.686 --> 00:56:14.156
I'm sorry.

890
00:56:14.206 --> 00:56:15.556
Why?

891
00:56:15.606 --> 00:56:18.156
Why does everybody think I am so scared?

892
00:56:18.206 --> 00:56:21.396
We all face the raven in
the end. That is the deal.

893
00:56:21.446 --> 00:56:23.996
If I go back to Gallifrey.
they can put me back. right?

894
00:56:24.046 --> 00:56:27.166
- On Trap Street. the moment
they took me out? - Of course.

895
00:56:29.046 --> 00:56:30.586
Mind you...

896
00:56:31.366 --> 00:56:33.036
.. seeing as I'm not actually ageing.

897
00:56:33.086 --> 00:56:35.356
there's a tiny little bit
of wiggle room. isn't there?

898
00:56:35.406 --> 00:56:37.436
- Wiggle room?
- Wiggle room.

899
00:56:37.486 --> 00:56:40.316
Yeah. you know. wiggle room.

900
00:56:40.366 --> 00:56:43.766
We could. erm. you know.
stop off on the way.

901
00:56:45.086 --> 00:56:46.836
- Where are we going?
- Gallifrey.

902
00:56:46.886 --> 00:56:48.726
Like I said...

903
00:56:50.166 --> 00:56:51.766
.. Gallifrey.

904
00:56:54.366 --> 00:56:56.306
The long way round.

905
00:59:53.476 --> 00:59:55.866
Is there anything on my head?

906
00:59:55.916 --> 00:59:57.586
Er. well. yes.

907
00:59:58.196 --> 00:59:59.306
Raver!

908
00:59:59.356 --> 01:00:01.156
Death initiating.

909
01:00:02.116 --> 01:00:04.466
Stop holding my hand!
People don't do that to me.

910
01:00:04.516 --> 01:00:06.026
Destroy them!

911
01:00:06.076 --> 01:00:07.706
Nobody move or the head gets it.

912
01:00:07.756 --> 01:00:10.796
A sonic trowel... You realise
how ridiculous that sounds?

913
01:00:12.796 --> 01:00:16.546
- You planned to take my head.
- It never crossed my mind.

914
01:00:16.596 --> 01:00:17.906
Long live the king!

915
01:00:17.956 --> 01:00:21.266
This is a serious mission. There
is nothing to laugh about here.

916
01:00:21.316 --> 01:00:23.186
We're being threatened by a bag!

917
01:00:23.236 --> 01:00:24.636
Give us the treasure!

918
01:00:25.305 --> 01:01:25.410
